# Pairs with ReadPositionHonest, and reproduces issue #4654: a leaf whose row is
# gone activates without a new-leaf intent. With its snapshot gone too (the
# second fault), nothing durable records that it ever held coverage, so it
# starts cold from the trimmed WAL and reads past an owned write it never
# holds. This is the pre-fix behaviour, and also a record-based fix that loses
# its record together with the row. The base fails closed unless a create path
# passes the intent.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestRowlessActivationStartsCold
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a rowless leaf activates cold without a create intent and replays a trimmed WAL
PERTURBS: Activate

--- FIND
    /\ row[l] \/ CreateIntent(l)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the new-leaf intent is not required.
    /\ TRUE
--- END
--- FIND
SnapshotLoss == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the environment may destroy a snapshot or a leaf row.
SnapshotLoss == TRUE
--- END

--- FIND
MaxFaults == 1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the row and the snapshot both vanish: two faults.
MaxFaults == 2
--- END